From e9c6c6c5a081b16047f53bf22f17c6a85655f479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tad <tad.keller@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:21:52 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] android: Drive a flash LED as a torch

A camera entry of the HAL configuration file can name the LED class
device of the camera's flash LED ("flash-led"). For such a camera report
the flash as available, implement the camera module's set_torch_mode()
while the camera is closed, and follow FLASH_MODE_TORCH in the capture
requests while it is open, reporting the flash state in the results.
Opening the camera turns the torch off and makes it unavailable until the
camera is closed, as the framework expects.

The LED class brightness levels are the torch strength levels
(FLASH_INFO_STRENGTH_MAXIMUM_LEVEL and DEFAULT_LEVEL, added to the
metadata definitions). The camera3 module API predates them, so the
module's library exports libcamera_hal_turn_on_torch_with_strength_level()
and libcamera_hal_get_torch_strength_level() for a camera provider to
implement turnOnTorchWithStrengthLevel() and getTorchStrengthLevel().
Android's flashlight tile only turns on a torch that has strength levels.
